{
  "domain": "k8s",
  "problems": [
    {
      "title": "kubectl: The connection to the server localhost:8080 was refused",
      "area": "kubectl / kubeconfig",
      "tool": "kubectl, kubeadm, k3s, Helm",
      "level": "L0",
      "context": "First command after kubeadm init, after sudo -i, on a worker node, in a CI job, or with Helm on k3s. kubectl found no kubeconfig and fell back to its built-in default of http://localhost:8080.",
      "error_text": "The connection to the server localhost:8080 was refused - did you specify the right host or port? | couldn't get current server API group list: Get \"http://localhost:8080/api?timeout=32s\": dial tcp 127.0.0.1:8080: connect: connection refused | Error: Kubernetes cluster unreachable: Get \"http://localhost:8080/version\"",
      "frequency_signal": "Most-viewed topic of all time on discuss.kubernetes.io (about 842k views, 76 replies). The API-group-list variant has about 160k views. k3s issue #1126 (Helm 3 'cluster unreachable') has 46 +1 reactions.",
      "root_causes": [
        "No kubeconfig for this user: kubeadm writes /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf, but it was never copied to ~/.kube/config, or you are now root or another user.",
        "kubectl run on a worker node, which has no admin kubeconfig.",
        "KUBECONFIG not exported in the shell, under sudo, in cron or in the CI job.",
        "k3s and RKE2 write a root-only kubeconfig to /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml or /etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.yaml. Helm and a separately installed kubectl don't look there."
      ],
      "diagnosis": [
        "kubectl config view --minify    # empty output means no kubeconfig was loaded",
        "echo $KUBECONFIG; ls -l ~/.kube/config",
        "sudo ls -l /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml /etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.yaml",
        "kubectl get nodes -v=6    # prints which config file and server URL it uses"
      ],
      "fix": [
        "kubeadm: mkdir -p $HOME/.kube && sudo cp -i /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf $HOME/.kube/config && sudo chown $(id -u):$(id -g) $HOME/.kube/config",
        "k3s: mkdir -p ~/.kube && sudo cp /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml ~/.kube/config && sudo chown $USER: ~/.kube/config && chmod 600 ~/.kube/config. Use --write-kubeconfig-mode 644 only on a lab box.",
        "For remote use, copy the file and change server: https://127.0.0.1:6443 to the node or VIP address.",
        "CI: store the kubeconfig as a file-type CI variable and export KUBECONFIG in the job."
      ],
      "prevention": "Give each admin their own kubeconfig instead of sharing admin.conf, name contexts clearly, and show the current context in the shell prompt (kube-ps1 or kubectx).",
      "sources": [
        {"title": "discuss.kubernetes.io: The connection to the server localhost:8080 was refused", "url": "https://discuss.kubernetes.io/t/the-connection-to-the-server-localhost-8080-was-refused-did-you-specify-the-right-host-or-port/1464", "type": "forum", "verified": true},
        {"title": "discuss.kubernetes.io: Couldn't get current server API group list (localhost:8080)", "url": "https://discuss.kubernetes.io/t/couldnt-get-current-server-api-group-list-get-http-localhost-8080-api-timeout-32s-dial-tcp-127-0-0-1-connect-connection-refused/25471", "type": "forum", "verified": true},
        {"title": "k3s #1126: Error: Kubernetes cluster unreachable with helm 3.0", "url": "https://github.com/k3s-io/k3s/issues/1126", "type": "github-issue", "verified": true},
        {"title": "Stack Overflow search", "url": "https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=%22connection+to+the+server+localhost%3A8080+was+refused%22", "type": "search", "verified": false}
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "kubeadm init fails or the control plane keeps restarting: containerd has CRI disabled or the wrong cgroup driver",
      "area": "containerd / kubeadm",
      "tool": "containerd, kubeadm, kubelet",
      "level": "L1",
      "context": "Fresh Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 node with containerd.io from Docker's apt repo or Ubuntu's containerd package. The packaged /etc/containerd/config.toml is written for Docker, not for Kubernetes.",
      "error_text": "[ERROR CRI]: container runtime is not running: ... rpc error: code = Unimplemented desc = unknown service runtime.v1.RuntimeService | later: kube-apiserver, etcd and the scheduler restart every few minutes, and 'The connection to the server <IP>:6443 was refused' comes and goes",
      "frequency_signal": "Classic in CKA labs and homelabs. The Kubernetes container-runtimes page warns that containerd installed from a package may ship with the CRI plugin disabled.",
      "root_causes": [
        "The packaged config.toml contains disabled_plugins = [\"cri\"], so kubeadm and kubelet cannot talk CRI to containerd.",
        "kubelet uses the systemd cgroup driver (the kubeadm default since v1.22) while containerd runs runc with SystemdCgroup = false (cgroupfs). On cgroup v2 hosts (Ubuntu 22.04+) this leads to sandbox restarts and a flapping control plane.",
        "Old cgroup v1 hosts: according to the v1.35+ release notes, recent kubelets refuse to start on cgroup v1 by default (failCgroupV1)."
      ],
      "diagnosis": [
        "sudo crictl --runtime-endpoint unix:///run/containerd/containerd.sock info | head",
        "grep -nE 'disabled_plugins|SystemdCgroup' /etc/containerd/config.toml",
        "stat -fc %T /sys/fs/cgroup    # cgroup2fs means cgroup v2",
        "sudo journalctl -u kubelet -b --no-pager | grep -iE 'cgroup|sandbox' | tail -20",
        "sudo crictl ps -a | grep -E 'kube-apiserver|etcd'    # a high attempt count means flapping"
      ],
      "fix": [
        "sudo mkdir -p /etc/containerd && containerd config default | sudo tee /etc/containerd/config.toml",
        "Set SystemdCgroup = true in the runc options of the file you just generated. containerd 1.7 uses config version 2 (plugins.\"io.containerd.grpc.v1.cri\"...runtimes.runc.options). containerd 2.x uses version 3 with different plugin names, so don't paste old snippets into a v3 file.",
        "sudo systemctl restart containerd && sudo systemctl restart kubelet",
        "If kubeadm init already half-ran: sudo kubeadm reset -f, then run init again."
      ],
      "prevention": "Template config.toml with Ansible, pin the containerd version, and keep kubelet cgroupDriver: systemd. Plan the move to containerd 2.x now: the current Kubernetes docs say kubelet's fallback for containerd 1.x (which lacks the RuntimeConfig RPC) is dropped in v1.38.",
      "sources": [
        {"title": "Kubernetes docs: Container Runtimes (cgroup drivers, containerd CRI plugin note)", "url": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/setup/production-environment/container-runtimes/", "type": "docs", "verified": true},
        {"title": "Kubernetes docs: Troubleshooting kubeadm", "url": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/setup/production-environment/tools/kubeadm/troubleshooting-kubeadm/", "type": "docs", "verified": true},
        {"title": "Stack Overflow search", "url": "https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=%22unknown+service+runtime.v1.RuntimeService%22", "type": "search", "verified": false},
        {"title": "Reddit r/kubernetes search", "url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/kubernetes/search/?q=SystemdCgroup+apiserver+restarting&restrict_sr=1", "type": "search", "verified": false}
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Node NotReady and CoreDNS Pending: cni plugin not initialized",
      "area": "CNI / kubeadm",
      "tool": "kubelet, Flannel, Calico, Cilium",
      "level": "L1",
      "context": "Right after kubeadm init or join, or after upgrading or removing a CNI.",
      "error_text": "container runtime network not ready: NetworkReady=false reason:NetworkPluginNotReady message:Network plugin returns error: cni plugin not initialized | failed to find plugin \"flannel\" in path [/opt/cni/bin] | coredns-xxxx 0/1 Pending",
      "frequency_signal": "kubeadm issue #1031 'runtime network not ready' has 72 comments. The kubeadm troubleshooting docs say CoreDNS stays Pending until a network add-on is installed.",
      "root_causes": [
        "No CNI installed yet. kubeadm doesn't pick one, so CoreDNS stays Pending by design.",
        "The CNI DaemonSet pod is failing on that node: image pull, RBAC, a pod CIDR mismatch or a missing kernel module.",
        "Binaries missing from /opt/cni/bin (flannel, bridge, loopback, portmap), or leftover config from a previous CNI in /etc/cni/net.d."
      ],
      "diagnosis": [
        "kubectl get nodes -o wide; kubectl describe node NODE | grep -A6 Conditions",
        "kubectl get pods -A -o wide | grep -Ei 'flannel|calico|cilium|coredns'    # Flannel runs in kube-flannel, operator-installed Calico in calico-system",
        "ls /etc/cni/net.d /opt/cni/bin",
        "sudo journalctl -u kubelet -b --no-pager | grep -i cni | tail -20"
      ],
      "fix": [
        "Install exactly one CNI whose pod CIDR matches kubeadm init --pod-network-cidr. Flannel's default is 10.244.0.0/16.",
        "If binaries are missing, install the CNI plugins into /opt/cni/bin (Ubuntu package containernetworking-plugins, or the upstream release tarball).",
        "When switching CNIs: delete the old DaemonSet, remove stale /etc/cni/net.d/* files on every node, then restart containerd and kubelet or reboot."
      ],
      "prevention": "Choose pod and service CIDRs before kubeadm init, write them down, and install the CNI as part of the bootstrap playbook.",
      "sources": [
        {"title": "kubeadm #1031: runtime network not ready: NetworkReady=false", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubeadm/issues/1031", "type": "github-issue", "verified": true},
        {"title": "Kubernetes docs: Troubleshooting kubeadm (coredns Pending, network add-on)", "url": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/setup/production-environment/tools/kubeadm/troubleshooting-kubeadm/", "type": "docs", "verified": true},
        {"title": "Stack Overflow search", "url": "https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=%22cni+plugin+not+initialized%22", "type": "search", "verified": false}
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The connection to the server <IP>:6443 was refused: the API server is down after a reboot or a change",
      "area": "kubeadm / control plane",
      "tool": "kubelet, kube-apiserver static pod, etcd, containerd",
      "level": "L2",
      "context": "The cluster worked yesterday. After a reboot, power cut, OS update, full disk or IP change, kubectl is refused on 6443. On a homelab with one control-plane node, everything stops.",
      "error_text": "The connection to the server 192.0.2.10:6443 was refused - did you specify the right host or port?",
      "frequency_signal": "Second most-viewed topic on discuss.kubernetes.io (about 592k views, 81 replies). kubeadm issue #1026 'kubelet won't restart after reboot' has 67 comments.",
      "root_causes": [
        "kubelet isn't running, and it is what starts the static pods. Typical reasons: swap turned back on by /etc/fstab, containerd down, or a broken kubelet config.",
        "etcd won't start (disk full, corrupt data, slow disk), so the API server crashes too.",
        "Control-plane certificates expired after about a year, or the node IP changed (DHCP or a netplan edit), so the advertise address and certificates no longer match.",
        "A cgroup driver mismatch makes the static pods restart over and over."
      ],
      "diagnosis": [
        "sudo systemctl status kubelet containerd --no-pager",
        "sudo journalctl -u kubelet -b -n 100 --no-pager",
        "sudo crictl ps -a | grep -E 'kube-apiserver|etcd'; sudo crictl logs CONTAINER_ID",
        "sudo ss -ltnp | grep 6443; swapon --show; df -h /var/lib/etcd; ip -4 addr",
        "sudo kubeadm certs check-expiration"
      ],
      "fix": [
        "Swap: sudo swapoff -a and comment out the swap line in /etc/fstab, unless you have configured NodeSwap on purpose.",
        "Start the runtime before kubelet: sudo systemctl restart containerd kubelet",
        "Expired certificates: sudo kubeadm certs renew all, restart the control-plane static pods, then copy /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf to ~/.kube/config again.",
        "Changed IP: give control-plane nodes static IPs (netplan or a DHCP reservation) and use a DNS name or VIP as controlPlaneEndpoint. Otherwise the certificates and manifests have to be regenerated."
      ],
      "prevention": "Use static IPs or DHCP reservations for nodes, set controlPlaneEndpoint to a DNS name from day one, alert on certificate expiry and disk usage, and write down a shutdown and startup order (drain, stop kubelet, then power off).",
      "sources": [
        {"title": "discuss.kubernetes.io: The connection to the server <host>:6443 was refused", "url": "https://discuss.kubernetes.io/t/the-connection-to-the-server-host-6443-was-refused-did-you-specify-the-right-host-or-port/552", "type": "forum", "verified": true},
        {"title": "kubeadm #1026: kubelet won't restart after reboot - connection refused", "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/kubeadm/issues/1026", "type": "github-issue", "verified": true},
        {"title": "Kubernetes docs: Troubleshooting kubeadm", "url": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/setup/production-environment/tools/kubeadm/troubleshooting-kubeadm/", "type": "docs", "verified": true},
        {"title": "Server Fault search", "url": "https://serverfault.com/search?q=%22connection+to+the+server%22+6443+refused", "type": "search", "verified": false}
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Nodes register with the wrong IP (multi-NIC servers, Vagrant 10.0.2.15): kubectl logs/exec fail and cross-node traffic breaks",
      "area": "kubeadm / node networking",
      "tool": "kubelet, Flannel, Calico",
      "level": "L2",
      "context": "Vagrant/VirtualBox labs, where every VM has the same NAT address 10.0.2.15 on eth0, and on-prem servers with separate management, storage or backup NICs.",
      "error_text": "kubectl get nodes -o wide shows the same INTERNAL-IP on every node | Error from server: error dialing backend: dial tcp 10.0.2.15:10250: connect: connection refused | pods on different nodes cannot reach each other",
      "frequency_signal": "The kubeadm troubleshooting docs give it two sections: the default NIC flannel picks under Vagrant, and a non-public IP being used for containers.",
      "root_causes": [
        "kubelet takes the IP of the interface that holds the default route, which may not be the cluster network.",
        "Flannel and Calico autodetect the first interface and build their tunnels over the wrong network."
      ],
      "diagnosis": [
        "kubectl get nodes -o wide",
        "ip -4 route get 1.1.1.1; ip -br addr",
        "kubectl -n kube-flannel logs ds/kube-flannel-ds | grep -i 'using interface'"
      ],
      "fix": [
        "Set the kubelet node IP on Ubuntu: echo 'KUBELET_EXTRA_ARGS=--node-ip=192.0.2.21' | sudo tee /etc/default/kubelet && sudo systemctl restart kubelet",
        "Pass kubeadm init --apiserver-advertise-address=CLUSTER_NIC_IP, and set node-ip under nodeRegistration.kubeletExtraArgs in the kubeadm config file.",
        "Flannel: add --iface=enp0s8 (or --iface-regex) to the kube-flannel container args. Calico: set nodeAddressAutodetectionV4 (see the cross-node traffic problem)."
      ],
      "prevention": "Keep node-ip in the kubeadm config you store in Git. In Vagrantfiles, give every VM a private_network IP and template node-ip from it.",
      "sources": [
        {"title": "Kubernetes docs: Troubleshooting kubeadm (Default NIC with flannel in Vagrant; Non-public IP used for containers)", "url": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/setup/production-environment/tools/kubeadm/troubleshooting-kubeadm/", "type": "docs", "verified": true},
        {"title": "Stack Overflow search", "url": "https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=kubernetes+node+internal+ip+10.0.2.15+vagrant", "type": "search", "verified": false},
        {"title": "Reddit r/kubernetes search", "url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/kubernetes/search/?q=node-ip+wrong+interface&restrict_sr=1", "type": "search", "verified": false}
      ]
    }
